WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.060
Five

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:01.060
Four

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:02.060
Three

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:03.060
Two

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:04.060
One

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:04.980
One!

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:14.040
Good morning!

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:34.570
Time to eat!

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:51.530
Aya

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:53.490
Tachibana
Aya

00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:59.410
Sae?

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:02.410
Just a minute.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.010
Yunocchi, what happened?

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:18.260
Sorry, Miya. You can go ahead without me.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:21.010
Oh man...

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:24.990
What's wrong? That was pretty loud.

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:26.090
Are you okay?

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:28.940
Sae, Hiro, I'm sorry.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.440
This sure is a mess.

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:37.070
Stick! Stick!

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:38.660
There we go.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:42.730
Man, you only end up doing this when we're in a hurry.

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:46.770
I thought I saw something dark under the fridge.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:49.830
I was wrong, but it still startled me.

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:51.480
Yeah, I hear you.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:53.090
Isn't this good enough?

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:56.050
Thanks for helping out.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.390
Ah, the time!

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:00.720
Oh no...

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:03.220
We're still okay.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:11.350
We can make it!

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:17.990
February 27th~March 4th

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:17.990
"Bright Red Mark"

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:19.990
Art Dept.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:19.990
We made it.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:23.280
It sure is nice living right next to school.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:24.110
Yeah.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.870
Hey, what are you doing Saturday?

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:27.840
You going anywhere?

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:31.040
We spent all last week on exams, didn't we?

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:34.090
Going to an amusement park or something would be great.

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:37.050
I want to go to the supermarket.

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:40.340
The supermarket? What are you going to buy?

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.220
Everything!

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:48.560
All right, I'm returning your exams now.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.850
The average score was fifty-five points.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:52.980
It must have been pretty tough.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.030
Those who scored below twenty-five will have to take the supplementary exam.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:59.610
The grammar this time was tough.

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:01.110
I wonder if I passed.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:03.320
I suck at grammar.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:08.660
Now that I think of it, what does grammar even mean?

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:10.540
It's the comparative form of gram, isn't it?

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:13.210
Gram, grammar, glamorous!

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.090
Glamorous!?

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:21.910
How'd you do, Miya?

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:24.890
Not that hot.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:26.220
That's scary.

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:42.910
Yunocchi?

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:48.030
With the completion of finals yesterday,

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:52.460
even though work remains, our hearts turn to spring break.

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:55.460
So, where shall we go this Saturday?

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.130
At that moment, suddenly—

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:00.590
A big red X on grammar. Supplementary exams next week.

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:02.970
Where has our relaxed mood gone?

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:15.230
Thus why Yuno's X's seem so much bigger than usual.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:19.090
Cheer up, Yuno.

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:21.740
Yeah, we're all here for you.

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:24.240
Thanks.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:28.620
Oh, I can give you my notes from last year. I think they'll help.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:30.740
Thank you.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:35.120
Leave the cooking to me. I'll bring you plenty of tasty meals.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:36.790
That'll help a lot.

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:41.420
I'll make you feel like you're at an amusement park!

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:43.800
Miya, that stings.

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:51.520
All right, let's go.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.430
Okay! Thanks for the help.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:57.420
Still, I can't believe you got a twenty-four.

00:04:57.420 --> 00:05:01.320
Twenty-five was the cutoff. I almost made it.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:04.650
Huh? They graded it wrong.

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:05.700
Really?

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.610
Yeah, there's a spelling error.

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:09.710
You should've gotten a twenty-two.

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:14.370
February 28th

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:17.330
Let's get some food in you.

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:21.570
Good work. Come on in.

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:24.120
Sorry to bother you during break.

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:25.090
It's fine, really.

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:32.510
Shall we have lunch?

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:34.060
Thanks, Hiro!

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:39.810
Udon!

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:43.190
All right, as soon as you name all of these in English, we can eat!

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:44.650
What? Even the dishes?

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:51.450
Um... Noodle, right? And soup, and chicken, and...

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:55.200
Kamaboko?

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.620
What's a kamaboko called?

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:57.870
Yunocchi, fight!

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:02.090
I don't think it would ever show up on a grammar test.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.050
Fish cake!

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:10.050
March 3rd

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:15.930
Oh my.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:22.770
Why are you studying? Exams are over.

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:24.270
Miss Yoshinoya.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:27.320
I'm studying grammar because I have to take the make-up exam.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:32.280
Grammar? English is my strong point!

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:34.700
Wow, it really is glamorous!

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:41.210
Ai rabu yuu.

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:41.210
What an incredible Japanese accent.

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:46.340
Doing better?

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:48.220
Yeah, thanks for all the help.

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:51.890
Why'd you do so bad on grammar, anyway?

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:57.470
I had Math I the same day, and I crammed for that.

00:06:57.470 --> 00:07:01.140
I see. So you at least did well on that?

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:05.320
I just got it back today.

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:10.240
A paper airplane?

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:12.320
Obviously not that great.

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:23.500
All right, one more question and that's it.

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:28.220
I was able to get a lot of studying done, thanks to everyone.

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:30.880
I think I'll do well on the make-up exam tomorrow.

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:34.300
Translate the text into English.

00:07:34.310 --> 00:07:38.020
If you drink that drink, you will feel ill.

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:55.730
It's almost over. I wonder if Yuno's doing okay.

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:57.660
I'm sure she's fine.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:03.500
Yu—

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:09.370
A student!

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:17.970
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.680
Yunocchi!

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.680
Yuno!

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:23.420
How'd you do?

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:26.940
Tadah!

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:30.780
It's all right.

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:36.030
Stick, stick, stick, stick...

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:43.960
Wow, getting a hundred is amazing!

00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:46.580
Thanks, but I did have to retake it.

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:48.960
Getting them all right is still impressive.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:54.550
Okay, dinner's ready. Let's eat.

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:56.810
Thanks.

00:08:56.810 --> 00:08:58.850
What did you make?

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:00.470
Stew!

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:04.480
Oh, stew.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:11.730
Potato, carrot, onion, broccoli, chicken, flour, butter...

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:14.740
Yuno, that's enough! That's more than enough!

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:14.820
Five

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:15.820
Four

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:16.820
Three

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:17.820
Two

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:18.820
One

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:19.740
One!

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:23.750
April 1st

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:28.170
It's already past midnight.

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:31.510
This really brings back so many memories.

00:09:31.510 --> 00:09:34.370
Your stew was so tasty.

00:09:34.370 --> 00:09:35.800
I'll make it again sometime.

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:39.930
Though I'd rather not get any more red X's.

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:39.930
Saitama Kumar Resort Special Issue

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:42.560
Let's go to an amusement park next time.

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:44.370
Yeah!

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:03.130
Full occupancy!

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:16.710
Good morning, Landlady.

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:20.260
Oh, you're sweeping up? Thanks a ton.

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:21.930
What are you here for today?

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:24.180
I came to clean up the empty rooms.

00:10:24.570 --> 00:10:27.020
There'll be first years moving in soon.

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:35.240
Um, um... First years other than us?

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:36.820
That's right, Miss Second Year.

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:44.250
Miya! Miya! Are you awake?

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:46.410
What's up, Yunocchi?

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:50.920
First years are moving into their new digs in the empty rooms!

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:52.670
That's big news!

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:57.380
Big news, Hiro!

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:59.550
Hidamari Apartments is getting dug up!

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:05.180
They're digging a hole for Hidamari Apartments?

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:07.850
What are you talking about?

00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:15.720
Oh, two first years are moving in?

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:17.710
So, all the rooms will be occupied?

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:20.940
Yeah, for the first time in three years.

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:23.530
I'll finally be able to live it up.

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:28.060
I can drink beer instead of happoshu, and have my favorite shochu every night.

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:31.850
I can have all the Dom rose I want!

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:35.000
Hey, if you have some free time, wanna help clean?

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:37.380
I'll make it worth your while.

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:45.500
Wow, it's dirty.

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:48.640
If you don't use a room, it gets dirty quick.

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:53.750
First years, huh?
I wonder what they'll be like.

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:57.650
They'll probably be taller than me.

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:01.780
Yeah, I think you're right.

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:09.160
Looking at this empty room reminds me of when I moved here.

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:11.370
Yeah, it's nostalgic.

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:18.630
To be honest, I thought we'd have a hard time getting along when I first met you.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:20.840
How about you?

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:22.380
I didn't really...

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:25.800
What? Didn't you have any first impressions?

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:30.560
She's gonna say there was nothing, nothing...

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:34.250
I thought you looked like a really sweet girl.

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:45.740
Hello! Lunch delivery!

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:48.370
Oh, it's here.

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:50.700
Sae, can you get the others from upstairs?

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:51.660
Sure.

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:57.080
You ordered out?

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:59.340
Yeah, as thanks for helping out.

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:00.920
It looks great.

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:04.670
Okay, we've got roast cutlet, chicken namban,

00:13:04.670 --> 00:13:09.550
demiglace burger, stirfried veggie, and the yakiniku special.

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:12.640
Pick whichever you want.

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:14.180
Okay!

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:20.490
Guess I figured that one would be left.

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:26.870
Oh, that's right.

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:29.230
I hooked up a net connection.

00:13:29.230 --> 00:13:31.700
If you want to go online, just ask.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:33.180
Net connection?

00:13:33.180 --> 00:13:36.210
Yeah, the girl in 103 wanted one.

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:38.960
So, she owns a computer?

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:42.090
Soon, Hidamari Apartments will be part of the IT revolution!

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:45.970
Miyako, do you know what IT stands for?

00:13:46.460 --> 00:13:48.350
In Ternet!

00:13:58.020 --> 00:14:02.070
Miss Yoshinoya! Did you hear the big news at Hidamari Apartments?

00:14:02.090 --> 00:14:05.090
Two first years are moving in!

00:14:05.090 --> 00:14:06.820
Ah, yes.

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:10.490
I'm also looking forward to meeting the new students.

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:13.240
I've been really busy preparing.

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:14.950
You too?

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:18.330
Tadah!

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:21.330
What are you going to do with that?

00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:24.520
Cleaning's done!

00:14:24.520 --> 00:14:26.210
Good work.

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:30.970
Landlady, when are they moving in?

00:14:32.030 --> 00:14:34.140
They're coming in the afternoon the day after tomorrow.

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:35.770
The day after tomorrow...

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:38.980
What should we do tomorrow?

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:44.400
Let's draw what we think they'll look like.

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:45.820
What for?

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:54.830
April 3rd
"Welcome to
Hidamari Apartments"

00:15:01.370 --> 00:15:02.790
You stressing, Yunocchi?

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:04.670
Yeah, a bit.

00:15:04.690 --> 00:15:08.310
What will they be like? Will we get along?

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:13.580
Do you remember a year ago when you came?

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:14.400
Yeah.

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:21.890
That's right. They must be even more nervous than us.

00:15:21.890 --> 00:15:24.340
I've gotta hang in there.

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:30.250
We took a bath together.

00:15:30.250 --> 00:15:32.570
Ah, nostalgia...

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:35.030
Oh, they're here!

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:37.330
Huh? But it's only a little after 9:00.

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:40.080
Nah, they really are.

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:46.340
Hurry up, Sae!

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:50.590
It's not like we have to meet them at the curb.

00:15:53.130 --> 00:15:55.260
Oh, are you the ones who live here?

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:58.140
Good morning. It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:15:58.140 --> 00:15:59.450
Huh?

00:16:04.830 --> 00:16:07.440
That's all the boxes. You set from here?

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:09.280
Yeah, we'll be fine.

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:12.580
Okay, we're done. Later.

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:14.190
Thank you.

00:16:14.190 --> 00:16:15.280
Thanks!

00:16:17.670 --> 00:16:21.850
We finished fast. There's still time before she gets here.

00:16:21.850 --> 00:16:23.540
Yeah.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:30.090
Hey, let's all go get something to eat!

00:16:56.290 --> 00:16:57.150
Huh?

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:31.520
H.S.

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:31.520
Transport

00:17:38.730 --> 00:17:40.320
Looks like we got here early.

00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:43.450
Mind if I go on ahead and say hi?

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:01.760
Huh? No one's here?

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:16.440
Man, I'm stuffed.

00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:18.690
Feels good.

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:22.180
I didn't think they'd take us out all of a sudden.

00:18:22.180 --> 00:18:25.330
They're nice, happy parents.

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:29.330
I wonder if their daughter is the IT revolutionary.

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:31.350
I wonder what they're like.

00:18:31.350 --> 00:18:34.300
Let's hurry back, put on some tea, and wait for them.

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:35.340
Yeah!

00:19:06.780 --> 00:19:08.960
What a mix-up.

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:13.000
We were supposed to greet them, but they ended up greeting us.

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:22.590
I hope I can get along with Nori and Nazuna.

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:27.870
Hello. Are you the girls from Hidamari Apartments?

00:19:27.870 --> 00:19:29.280
Ah, yes!

00:19:29.280 --> 00:19:30.420
I thought so.

00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:30.840
Um...

00:19:30.840 --> 00:19:36.570
Oh, you got here too? Say thanks to your parents for us.

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:39.750
We just had lunch with them. It was great.

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:40.970
Huh? Why?

00:19:40.970 --> 00:19:42.890
It just kind of happened that way.

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:44.700
Um, and you are...?

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:48.040
I'm Nazuna. I moved into 203.

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:51.160
So, you're new too? I'm glad there's someone my age.

00:19:51.180 --> 00:19:53.920
My name is Nori. I'm in 103.

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:57.640
Nice to meet you. I'm Yuno from room 201.

00:19:57.640 --> 00:19:59.530
Miyako from 202.

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:02.980
Yuno and Miyako are second years. We're third years.

00:20:02.980 --> 00:20:05.030
I'm Sae from room 102.

00:20:05.030 --> 00:20:06.720
I'm Hiro. Nice to meet you.

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:07.970
Pleased to meet you.

00:20:08.090 --> 00:20:09.490
Pleased to meet you.

00:20:09.490 --> 00:20:13.870
Our stuff's scattered all over. We must seem so stressed out.

00:20:13.870 --> 00:20:15.710
Oh, don't worry about it.

00:20:15.710 --> 00:20:17.960
How about having tea in my room to calm down?

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:19.330
Yeah, let's all have some together.

00:20:19.330 --> 00:20:22.570
Is it okay? I'll come by later, then.

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:24.100
Ah, um, me too.

00:20:24.100 --> 00:20:25.570
Okay. We'll be waiting.

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:31.250
Um, I know it'll be tough until you calm down, but if you need anything, just ask.

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:31.710
Okay!

00:20:31.710 --> 00:20:32.950
Thank you.

00:20:32.950 --> 00:20:35.920
You're welcome. Let's get along.

00:20:41.020 --> 00:20:43.220
Let's think of three great things about Hidamari Apartments!

